WEBVTT

00:00:00.680 --> 00:00:03.600
I'm gonna be the first-star idol one day!

00:00:03.600 --> 00:00:07.730
Nijino Yume's about to start her Aikatsu!

00:00:10.230 --> 00:00:13.820
If you want to fight off the summer heat

00:00:13.820 --> 00:00:16.660
all you need to do is eat one of these!

00:00:16.660 --> 00:00:20.790
Create your own miracle! Felici-taiyaki!

00:00:18.240 --> 00:00:18.830
Miracle!

00:00:23.830 --> 00:00:26.210
And cut! We're good!

00:00:26.500 --> 00:00:27.960
Good work.

00:00:27.960 --> 00:00:30.130
That was fantastic.

00:00:30.130 --> 00:00:31.920
Thank you!

00:00:33.010 --> 00:00:39.010
Apologies for bringing you all the way out here
so early on the day of Summer Fest.

00:00:39.010 --> 00:00:42.180
It's the least I could do for Koukadou considering all you've done for me.

00:00:43.520 --> 00:00:45.980
I'm pleased to know you feel that way.

00:00:45.980 --> 00:00:48.770
I'm looking forward to seeing you on stage with Hime-chan—

00:00:48.770 --> 00:00:49.770
Big problem, President!

00:00:50.190 --> 00:00:51.860
What is it?

00:00:51.860 --> 00:00:53.030
It's horrible!

00:02:32.090 --> 00:02:36.710
What?! What do you mean you can't come back, baby?

00:02:37.170 --> 00:02:40.720
The camera had a fault and didn't record anything.

00:02:40.720 --> 00:02:45.470
We're going to wait for a replacement part and record it again. {which is really weird, because it was clearly a sunrise setting}{sorry, but rerecord sees too oddly out}

00:02:45.470 --> 00:02:49.350
So does it look like you'll be able to make it back in time for the show?

00:02:49.350 --> 00:02:51.730
I can't say for sure.

00:02:54.570 --> 00:02:57.110
Have everyone on standby and ready to record.

00:02:57.110 --> 00:02:57.860
Understood.

00:03:00.570 --> 00:03:01.320
Sakuraba?

00:03:01.320 --> 00:03:02.620
R-Right!

00:03:03.120 --> 00:03:06.870
I'll definitely make it back in time for my performance with Hime-senpai!

00:03:06.870 --> 00:03:08.200
I promise!

00:03:09.290 --> 00:03:11.870
Got it. Keep us updated.

00:03:15.670 --> 00:03:18.090
Anna-sensei, what happened to Rola?

00:03:18.090 --> 00:03:20.630
She's going to be stuck for a while.

00:03:20.630 --> 00:03:25.140
That's awful! Rola was so looking forward to this.

00:03:25.140 --> 00:03:26.680
Now that it's come to this, {in cases/we will didn't match, or rather it wasn't quite there}

00:03:27.890 --> 00:03:32.400
we will need to prepare Song Class for the worst-case scenario.{lyger hyphen, best hyphen?}

00:03:32.400 --> 00:03:34.730
Worst-case scenario?

00:03:35.270 --> 00:03:37.900
Where Sakuraba can't make it back in time.

00:03:40.990 --> 00:03:43.530
I don't mind putting off the filming for another day.

00:03:43.530 --> 00:03:45.780
No. The show may be important,

00:03:45.780 --> 00:03:48.540
but this is also a big part of my Aikatsu.

00:03:48.540 --> 00:03:50.120
Still...

00:03:50.120 --> 00:03:53.710
Sorry for the delay. The new equipment just arrived.

00:03:56.000 --> 00:03:57.040
Step on it.

00:03:57.040 --> 00:03:58.420
We will!

00:03:59.840 --> 00:04:02.380
<i>Theater Class goes on in an hour.</i>

00:04:03.050 --> 00:04:04.760
<i>Once they're done...</i>

00:04:16.230 --> 00:04:17.820
What? Not Rola! {as in "that couldn't have happened to laura today of all days"}

00:04:17.820 --> 00:04:19.440
Is she okay?

00:04:19.440 --> 00:04:21.570
It's going to start soon!

00:04:22.400 --> 00:04:26.450
But I guess Hime-senpai could probably handle it solo.

00:04:26.450 --> 00:04:29.370
Yeah, she'd never lose to the other classes.

00:04:29.370 --> 00:04:30.240
Not true.

00:04:36.080 --> 00:04:37.590
Hime-senpai!

00:04:38.250 --> 00:04:42.470
The unprecedented pairing of S4 members and first-year students

00:04:42.470 --> 00:04:45.340
has brought the audience's hype to a peak. {I know this formation is don't like but gargantuan?}

00:04:45.970 --> 00:04:49.510
Anyone who would betray those expectations has no right to call herself an idol.

00:04:49.510 --> 00:04:51.720
Yes! That's exactly right.

00:04:52.890 --> 00:04:54.020
Okay...

00:04:56.230 --> 00:05:02.240
Didn't you all see Kasumi Yozora-san and Mahiru-san's performance yesterday?

00:05:02.240 --> 00:05:03.400
Yes!

00:05:03.400 --> 00:05:04.990
They were incredible!

00:05:05.700 --> 00:05:11.490
It would be impossible for me to surpass them without the power of someone beside me.

00:05:11.870 --> 00:05:16.370
But what are we going to do? There isn't time to go through the whole process—

00:05:16.370 --> 00:05:18.330
I have an idea regarding that.

00:05:19.960 --> 00:05:25.340
Since Rola-chan got first on the aptitude test, it would only make sense to ask second place.

00:05:25.340 --> 00:05:28.260
Well put. As for the girl in second...

00:05:28.260 --> 00:05:30.470
It's Nijino Yume!

00:05:33.020 --> 00:05:34.770
Let's hold a meeting right away.

00:05:34.770 --> 00:05:36.810
Find me in the Hall's waiting room. {Grand Hall, ep 11}

00:05:39.190 --> 00:05:41.360
O-Okay...

00:05:41.360 --> 00:05:43.480
Yume-chan, congrats!

00:05:47.780 --> 00:05:50.280
Done, for real.

00:05:50.660 --> 00:05:53.830
We actually have it now. Well done!

00:05:53.830 --> 00:05:55.290
Good job!

00:05:54.370 --> 00:05:55.290
Thank you!

00:05:55.290 --> 00:05:57.210
Thank you, everyone.

00:05:57.210 --> 00:06:00.040
We couldn't have done this without you!

00:06:00.040 --> 00:06:02.460
Let's clean up, on the double!

00:06:02.460 --> 00:06:03.750
Okay!

00:06:03.750 --> 00:06:07.340
Rola-chan, we'll drive you back to the academy in our van.

00:06:07.340 --> 00:06:08.930
Will you really?

00:06:08.930 --> 00:06:11.550
It's the least we can do, right?

00:06:12.180 --> 00:06:13.890
Thank you!

00:06:15.220 --> 00:06:19.190
As soon as Theater Class finishes their piece, we'll do the final choreography check.

00:06:19.190 --> 00:06:22.190
There's no time, so I'm expecting you to get on it.

00:06:22.190 --> 00:06:23.150
Understood.

00:06:26.610 --> 00:06:27.740
Hey, Nijino.

00:06:27.740 --> 00:06:29.070
Y-Yes?

00:06:29.070 --> 00:06:30.990
Can you handle this?

00:06:30.990 --> 00:06:33.700
I can. B-But...

00:06:35.290 --> 00:06:39.170
Rola had a meeting with Hime-senpai yesterday too.

00:06:39.170 --> 00:06:42.840
If she makes it back in time, you'll let her go on, right?

00:06:42.840 --> 00:06:44.840
Of course, if she does...

00:06:45.550 --> 00:06:48.380
I'm going to wait for her at the main entrance!

00:06:48.380 --> 00:06:49.380
W-Wait!

00:06:49.380 --> 00:06:50.630
Nijino!

00:06:59.310 --> 00:07:02.100
Theater Class's show just started.

00:07:04.320 --> 00:07:05.650
Hey everyone!

00:07:05.650 --> 00:07:09.030
Thank you so much for coming to see us today.

00:07:10.150 --> 00:07:13.410
And with me today is...

00:07:13.410 --> 00:07:16.040
I-I'm Saotome Ako.

00:07:16.040 --> 00:07:19.290
It's an honor to be able to sing before you doday.

00:07:20.160 --> 00:07:22.420
Goodness me, I slipped over my words.

00:07:26.750 --> 00:07:27.800
Are you nervous?

00:07:27.800 --> 00:07:29.880
Th-That's not...

00:07:29.880 --> 00:07:32.930
...e-entirely untrue.{this is oddly reminiscent of the way I translated hime's "sonna koto aru kedo" in hacha}{that's the point, yep}

00:07:33.760 --> 00:07:36.060
<i>Excellent work, Saotome.</i>

00:07:36.640 --> 00:07:40.310
<i>Your hesitant and scaredy-cat acting is far beyond that of a first-year.</i>

00:07:41.190 --> 00:07:42.190
<i>It's splendid.</i>

00:07:44.190 --> 00:07:45.190
Isn't that right?

00:07:45.190 --> 00:07:46.360
Yeah.

00:07:47.780 --> 00:07:53.070
<i>Tsubasa-senpai can project such reassurance with one glance of the eye.</i>

00:07:53.070 --> 00:07:55.740
<i>I'm proud to have her lead Theater Class.</i>

00:07:57.030 --> 00:07:58.080
Get ready!

00:07:58.080 --> 00:08:02.620
Let us raise the curtain on a performance only the Theater Class can do!

00:08:02.620 --> 00:08:04.750
Okay, I'll do my best!

00:08:05.330 --> 00:08:09.710
But have I truly the ability to stand by your side?

00:08:09.710 --> 00:08:12.090
Don't worry, I'm here for you.

00:08:12.090 --> 00:08:14.510
Ts-Tsubasa-senpai! {actually, how do you stutter this?}{it looks weird, but only because ts-initial doesn't exist in native english words}

00:08:14.510 --> 00:08:16.390
Shall we take flight?

00:08:16.390 --> 00:08:20.020
Off into the endless blue skies!

00:08:20.020 --> 00:08:21.060
Yes!

00:08:26.610 --> 00:08:28.110
What's going on?

00:08:28.110 --> 00:08:31.110
We haven't moved in minutes.

00:08:31.110 --> 00:08:34.780
Sorry, it looks like there was an accident up ahead.

00:08:36.070 --> 00:08:37.910
<i>Our last rehearsal... {could use dress rehearsal but I think that's normally for plays}</i>

00:08:42.460 --> 00:08:45.120
I'll take the train the rest of the way back!

00:08:47.000 --> 00:08:48.790
Thank you for everything!

00:08:48.790 --> 00:08:50.630
Rola-chan!

00:09:02.680 --> 00:09:03.810
Rola...

00:09:05.600 --> 00:09:06.810
Yume-chan.

00:09:08.520 --> 00:09:12.530
I heard Rola hasn't made it back yet. {I understand but I don't like koharu saying it}

00:09:13.240 --> 00:09:14.240
Yeah...

00:09:20.200 --> 00:09:22.040
Theater Class's show...

00:09:22.580 --> 00:09:24.330
Sounds like it's over.

00:09:26.290 --> 00:09:27.290
No way...

00:09:27.290 --> 00:09:29.790
Due to a signal failure,

00:09:29.790 --> 00:09:33.300
the trains have been delayed for twenty to thirty minutes.

00:09:34.590 --> 00:09:40.050
We sincerely apologize for the inconvenience.

00:09:42.810 --> 00:09:43.560
Rola!

00:09:44.140 --> 00:09:45.680
Hello, Rola?

00:09:46.560 --> 00:09:48.190
Are you almost here?

00:09:49.770 --> 00:09:51.570
I can't really hear you.

00:09:51.940 --> 00:09:53.070
Yume.

00:09:54.150 --> 00:09:56.070
I have a favor to ask.

00:10:06.160 --> 00:10:07.960
You can't be serious!

00:10:07.960 --> 00:10:10.460
What do you mean you won't make it?

00:10:10.460 --> 00:10:11.960
It's unfortunately true.

00:10:13.250 --> 00:10:14.420
But why?!

00:10:14.960 --> 00:10:17.470
I won't accept that, Rola!

00:10:17.470 --> 00:10:19.390
What won't you accept?

00:10:19.390 --> 00:10:22.470
You've worked so hard all this time.

00:10:22.470 --> 00:10:25.470
I know that better than anyone else!

00:10:26.390 --> 00:10:28.480
Even though you were lost and confused,

00:10:28.480 --> 00:10:32.440
you still carried on with your Aikatsu and made it this far.

00:10:33.230 --> 00:10:35.400
I can't do it!

00:10:35.400 --> 00:10:38.740
I refuse to let all your hard work go to waste!

00:10:40.450 --> 00:10:41.700
Rola?

00:10:41.700 --> 00:10:43.240
What's this?

00:10:43.700 --> 00:10:45.620
That's all that was worrying you?

00:10:45.620 --> 00:10:47.370
What do you mean, that's all?

00:10:47.370 --> 00:10:50.420
Yume, hold out the palm of your right hand.{fun fact, I cannot pronounce the word tenohira}{I know, you sang that one song in TAB karaoke}

00:10:54.590 --> 00:10:55.800
Like this?

00:10:55.800 --> 00:10:57.720
Now raise it above your head.

00:11:00.050 --> 00:11:01.140
Like this?

00:11:01.760 --> 00:11:04.560
Ready? Then let's do it!

00:11:04.560 --> 00:11:05.640
Here we go!

00:11:05.640 --> 00:11:07.890
Aikatsu!

00:11:13.060 --> 00:11:14.690
I know about you too.

00:11:15.900 --> 00:11:19.110
About how much effort you put in every day.

00:11:20.240 --> 00:11:22.660
The rest is up to you!

00:11:35.420 --> 00:11:37.000
Yume-chan?

00:11:38.630 --> 00:11:39.760
Koharu-chan.

00:11:40.510 --> 00:11:42.090
I'm going to sing.

00:11:42.090 --> 00:11:43.300
What?

00:11:43.640 --> 00:11:46.810
I'm going to sing for both myself and Rola!

00:11:47.970 --> 00:11:48.810
Yeah.

00:11:49.480 --> 00:11:51.560
I know you can do it.

00:11:52.020 --> 00:11:53.100
See you later!

00:11:53.650 --> 00:11:55.060
Trust in yourself!{I... guess}

00:11:56.110 --> 00:11:57.940
Then, Rola-chan...

00:11:58.280 --> 00:12:00.780
There's no chance she'll be able to make it.

00:12:03.280 --> 00:12:04.450
Sorry for being late!

00:12:04.820 --> 00:12:07.830
Nijino Yume, returned and ready!

00:12:09.410 --> 00:12:12.080
Thank you for coming, Yume-chan.

00:12:12.080 --> 00:12:13.000
Of course.

00:12:13.750 --> 00:12:17.340
We have half an hour for 
the rehearsal. Can you handle it?

00:12:18.210 --> 00:12:20.210
Yes, I'll blow you out of the water!

00:12:21.220 --> 00:12:22.760
Good answer.

00:12:22.760 --> 00:12:24.760
Let's get this started.

00:12:24.760 --> 00:12:26.220
Okay!

00:12:26.220 --> 00:12:30.720
One, two! One, two!

00:12:30.720 --> 00:12:33.230
Nijino, you're a step too slow!

00:12:33.560 --> 00:12:34.690
Okay!

00:12:36.440 --> 00:12:37.400
<i>Rola.</i>

00:12:38.480 --> 00:12:40.530
<i>Rola believes in me.</i>

00:12:41.530 --> 00:12:43.860
<i>She passed me the baton!</i>

00:12:45.160 --> 00:12:47.490
<i>The rest is up to you!</i>

00:12:53.910 --> 00:12:56.420
<i>As the representative of all the Song Class first-years,</i>

00:12:57.540 --> 00:12:59.340
<i>and as Rola's replacement,</i>

00:13:02.130 --> 00:13:04.130
<i>I'll put on a show to be proud of.</i>

00:13:05.380 --> 00:13:09.140
<i>I swear, I swear...</i>

00:13:09.140 --> 00:13:10.390
<i>I'll pull this off!</i>

00:13:14.390 --> 00:13:16.770
All right, ten minutes left now.

00:13:17.440 --> 00:13:23.280
Let's finish this off by playing the backing track and going at concert tempo.

00:13:23.780 --> 00:13:26.030
Nijino, can you keep up?

00:13:26.660 --> 00:13:28.660
Yes, please start it!

00:13:31.160 --> 00:13:32.950
Wh-What is it?

00:13:33.500 --> 00:13:34.660
It's strange.

00:13:35.540 --> 00:13:39.290
Just now, it felt as though all three of us were dancing together.

00:13:40.170 --> 00:13:41.750
Three of us?

00:13:41.750 --> 00:13:44.050
Deep in your eyes,{if your name wasn't already attached to an editing thing, this would be it}{I think I get it actually}

00:13:44.760 --> 00:13:46.220
I could see Rola-chan.

00:13:47.340 --> 00:13:48.550
Rola was...

00:13:49.720 --> 00:13:50.800
Right!

00:13:55.390 --> 00:13:58.440
Ladies and gentlemen!

00:13:58.850 --> 00:14:02.440
I have a bit of unfortunate information for you all.{so the reason it's information and not news is that we keep her gratuitous english as a policy right}{y-yeah}

00:14:02.860 --> 00:14:10.240
Due to a minor accident, Sakuraba Rola will be unable to perform in the upcoming Song Class concert.

00:14:11.660 --> 00:14:13.450
We've called in a pinch hitter,{pinch hitter implies subbing}

00:14:13.450 --> 00:14:18.710
and it will be her fellow first-year, Nijino Yume, who will be singing with Shiratori Hime!

00:14:18.710 --> 00:14:21.460
So get ready to get it on!

00:14:23.500 --> 00:14:24.380
Oh?

00:14:28.090 --> 00:14:29.340
Girls.

00:14:29.340 --> 00:14:31.350
It was a little last-minute.

00:14:31.350 --> 00:14:34.430
See, we had to patch over this part. Sorry!

00:14:34.430 --> 00:14:36.560
We'll be cheering for you!

00:14:36.560 --> 00:14:38.690
Do your best, Yume-chan!

00:14:39.350 --> 00:14:41.610
Yeah, I'll give it my best shot!

00:14:41.610 --> 00:14:43.900
Thank you, everyone.

00:14:43.900 --> 00:14:45.650
Yume-chan, let's go.

00:14:45.650 --> 00:14:46.440
Okay.

00:14:47.030 --> 00:14:48.490
Bye, girls.

00:14:48.490 --> 00:14:49.660
See you after.

00:14:49.660 --> 00:14:51.490
Good luck!

00:14:53.700 --> 00:14:54.870
Good luck.

00:14:56.450 --> 00:14:57.660
Mahiru-chan?

00:14:58.290 --> 00:15:02.290
I'm light-years away from being a match for my sister.{it feels like a waste repeating english words when she's using new japanese ones}

00:15:02.290 --> 00:15:06.510
Even so, I put all I had into catching up with her. {or similar}{she's talking about today specifically}

00:15:07.170 --> 00:15:08.880
I want to see the same from you.

00:15:09.630 --> 00:15:12.140
Show me all Song Class has to offer.

00:15:13.470 --> 00:15:14.600
Thank you!

00:15:17.220 --> 00:15:18.600
Trust in yourself.

00:15:24.400 --> 00:15:29.440
<i>Rola, please lend me a bit of your strength.</i>

00:15:31.320 --> 00:15:34.530
Like a butterfly, like a fairy. {someone's channeling little fairy tales}

00:15:34.530 --> 00:15:38.700
Shall we begin our Song Class's show?

00:15:38.700 --> 00:15:39.450
Yes!

00:19:09.370 --> 00:19:12.130
You were amazing, Yume-chan!

00:19:14.630 --> 00:19:17.380
Yume-chan, you rock!

00:19:18.840 --> 00:19:20.800
You did it, Yume.

00:19:26.970 --> 00:19:32.900
It's time to announce the results from the Summer Fest unit performances.{good made this meal}

00:19:33.610 --> 00:19:39.400
Both the live vote and the remote votes have been tabulated.{so votes, not powerlevel}{you don't must results just because kekka you know}

00:19:54.500 --> 00:19:56.880
Wh-What is the meaning of this?

00:19:58.340 --> 00:20:00.670
Too bad for you, Tsubasacchi!

00:20:00.670 --> 00:20:02.590
I won't lose next time.

00:20:02.590 --> 00:20:05.140
Victory belongs to Dance Class!

00:20:08.930 --> 00:20:12.890
No way! Haruka's excitement is down, down! {just words. also I realized she calls herself haruka instead of luka?}

00:20:13.770 --> 00:20:18.190
Who do you believe the goddess of victory will smile down upon? {so there is technically a Goddess of Victory, this would be the relatively equivalent english version, but it's not quite the same. which do you think?}{shouri no megami is literally a reference to victoria/nike so it's actually exactly the same. definitely not lady luck. you could also do capital-V Victory if you wanted to write like a poetic dead person and give the goddess a name}

00:20:18.190 --> 00:20:20.690
Who can ever tell?

00:20:20.690 --> 00:20:23.950
She is known to be fickle.

00:20:37.790 --> 00:20:43.380
With this, Song Class has won Summer Fest.

00:20:47.800 --> 00:20:49.890
W-We did it!

00:20:49.890 --> 00:20:51.220
Congratulations!

00:20:51.220 --> 00:20:53.230
Congrats, Yume-chan!

00:20:56.810 --> 00:20:59.400
Congratulations, Yume-chan.

00:20:59.400 --> 00:21:00.690
Thank you!

00:21:00.690 --> 00:21:04.200
I suppose I can congratulate you for now.

00:21:04.650 --> 00:21:08.580
But you'll be the one saying it to me next time.

00:21:10.080 --> 00:21:11.580
Thanks...

00:21:11.580 --> 00:21:15.710
Honestly, that's an unsatisfying margin you beat Beauty Class by.

00:21:18.340 --> 00:21:19.710
Rola!

00:21:19.710 --> 00:21:21.090
If it were me up there,

00:21:21.090 --> 00:21:24.130
I'd have won by a landslide.

00:21:25.680 --> 00:21:26.890
Rola...

00:21:26.890 --> 00:21:28.600
Oh, that's right.

00:21:28.930 --> 00:21:33.270
Do you mind sharing that one month free lunch voucher with me? {should've used voucher instead of coupon last episode...}{truly}

00:21:37.600 --> 00:21:40.110
Of course, Rola!

00:21:40.820 --> 00:21:42.030
Rola!

00:21:43.360 --> 00:21:47.860
Ring ding-a-ling! The winner of this year's Summer Fest {channeling the Maria}

00:21:47.860 --> 00:21:49.660
was Song Class!

00:21:49.660 --> 00:21:51.160
Congratulations, Hime.

00:21:51.160 --> 00:21:52.700
Yay!

00:21:53.830 --> 00:21:55.750
Thank you, girls.

00:21:55.750 --> 00:21:58.420
